# Version Conversion: SemVer to PEP 440

## Conversion Function

The code converts Cargo.toml's SemVer version to PEP 440 using this approach:

```rust
let version = Version::from_str(&package.version.to_string()).map_err(|err| {
    format_err!(
        "Rust version used in Cargo.toml is not a valid python version: {}. \
            Note that rust uses [SemVer](https://semver.org/) while python uses \
            [PEP 440](https://peps.python.org/pep-0440/), which have e.g. some differences \
            when declaring prereleases.",
        err
    )
})?;
```

The `pep440_rs::Version` type handles the actual parsing and conversion from SemVer strings to PEP 440–compliant versions.

## Escaping and Encoding

For wheel filenames, hyphens are replaced with underscores:

```rust
pub fn get_version_escaped(&self) -> String {
    self.version.to_string().replace('-', "_")
}
```

## Dynamic Version Handling

When `pyproject.toml` contains a `[project]` section with an explicit `version` field, it overrides the Cargo.toml version:

```rust
if let Some(version) = &project.version {
    self.version = version.clone();
}
```

The metadata respects `project.dynamic` declarations—if version isn't listed as dynamic, it uses only the pyproject value, not Cargo.toml's.

